{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/299763-native-american-changelings","id":299763,"title":"Native American changelings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-01T23:54:11-07:00","id":299763,"title":"Native American changelings","content":"So I will run a episodic game set in New England. It will center on the rebuilding the tiny freehold in small town in Maine. As I thought about <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/298980-%E2%80%8Bhow-seasons-communicate-with-the-lost\">how could PCs &quot;reinvent&quot; Seasonal Courts on themselves</a>, I got also other idea - what if they found traces of much older Losts settlements. But looking as European were here only past last 400 years, easily they should found evidence of Native American freeholds. As Seasonal Courts are very Old World-centric phenomena I asking - <b>would original Courts of America be Seasons, or other ideas ( especially on USA/Canada border)? Were they described somewhere in the game line?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-02-2014, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T00:25:16-07:00","id":299789,"title":"","content":"I went with Directional courts, in my games. I changed the animals to wolf, eagle, snake, and bear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T01:39:10-08:00","id":299850,"title":"","content":"I believe the Dusk and Dawn Courts are Native American?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T02:28:37-08:00","id":299870,"title":"","content":"I just wonder how pre-Columbian exchange local Changelings fended off local Gentry without any substantial access to iron (I don't preclude iron from meteorites, but that would be rare indeed).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T04:34:06-08:00","id":299912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/299763-native-american-changelings?p=299870#post299870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just wonder how pre-Columbian exchange local Changelings fended off local Gentry without any substantial access to iron (I don't preclude iron from meteorites, but that would be rare indeed).</div> </div> </div> </div>Goblin markets, trading with European changelings through the Hedge?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T04:43:28-08:00","id":299914,"title":"","content":"Except it's basically the same as asking &quot;I wonder how Changelings fended off the Gentry before the Iron Age?&quot;<br /> <br /> Presumably, they relied more upon magic, stealth, and trickery than they did brute strength. Iron has never struck me as being all that integral to a Freehold's defence. It's fantastic if you need to try and hold your own against one of the Fae, but isn't the whole premise of a Freehold to try and make it so that such a situation never occurs?<br /> <br /> And, of course, it's entirely probable that they were a little less effective than modern Freeholds due to the lack of that defensive mechanism. It would mean that when every other line of defence fails, they didn't have iron weapons to fall back on. Not a huge deal in everyday life, but it would make the emergencies that much worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T05:24:17-08:00","id":299923,"title":"","content":"Or since legends are diverse across cultures, American Fae had different crippling weakness than iron. Jade comes to my mind as a stone of great importance for pre-Columbian cultures, at least in Central America.<br /> <br /> Which could have serious implications if Changelings from non-native cultures encountered those American Fae and had to fall back on cold iron when exhausting all options. And it does not work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T06:19:39-08:00","id":299939,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Iroquois_fairies_from_Stories_the_Iroquois_Tell_Their_Children_by_Mabel_Powers_1917.jpg/330px-Iroquois_fairies_from_Stories_the_Iroquois_Tell_Their_Children_by_Mabel_Powers_1917.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/How_Morning_Star_Lost_her_Fish_-_from_Stories_the_Iroquois_Tell_Their_Children_by_Mabel_Powers_1917.jpg/330px-How_Morning_Star_Lost_her_Fish_-_from_Stories_the_Iroquois_Tell_Their_Children_by_Mabel_Powers_1917.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <b><i>Native American &quot;Little People&quot; from Stories the Iroquois Tell Their Children by Mabel Powers 1917<br /> <br /> From wikipedia</i></b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T07:33:28-08:00","id":299968,"title":"","content":"In the oWoD, they had a book about the Nunnehi. The Nunnehi were fae from various Native American mythologies. You may wish to mine that as a resource.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T07:43:27-08:00","id":299992,"title":"","content":"Uh, I would rather mine Native American legends as firsthand as I could, because otherwise it's filtered through writing of RPG book wriers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T08:41:24-08:00","id":300026,"title":"","content":"I would do so also, Kat. Just that sometimes some people need a head start or jumping off point. I have been intrigued by some things mentioned in WoD books (classic and new) to research things and then come up with even more interesting tidbits and story ideas. I didn't say &quot;convert it directly&quot; but just to use it as a resource to mine for ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T09:38:46-08:00","id":300119,"title":"","content":"It is a good starting point; <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/N%C3%BB%C3%B1n%C3%AB&#39;h%C3%AF\" target=\"_blank\">N\u00fb\u00f1n\u00eb'h\u00ef</a><br /> <i><br /> The <b>Nunnehi</b> are a race of immortal spirit people in Cherokee folklore. In the Cherokee language, <i>Nunnehi</i> literally means &quot;The People Who Live Anywhere&quot;, but it is often translated into English as &quot;The People Who Live Forever&quot;, or simply &quot;The Immortals&quot;. The Cherokee believed the Nunnehi to be a type of supernatural human being, completely distinct from ghosts and nature spirits, as well as from gods. In this sense, the Nunnehi (along with the <i>Yunwi Tsunsdi</i>, or &quot;Little People&quot; in the Cherokee language) are the Cherokee equivalent of fairies in traditional European folklore. The belief in fairy-like beings is universal among all races, including all American Indian tribes.</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T09:41:54-08:00","id":300120,"title":"","content":"Thanks, that's a good starting point indeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T20:51:47-08:00","id":300698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1U2mJxUqoWBivwo1Jns-SgXYV217JCrHmU_S2hkmra7I/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1U2mJxUqoWBivwo1Jns-SgXYV217JCrHmU_S2hkmra7I/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1U2mJxUqoWBivwo1Jns-SgXYV217JCrHmU_S2hkmra7I/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1U2mJxUqoWBivwo1Jns-SgXYV217JCrHmU_S2hkmra7I/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I use this thingy to some degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T19:59:43-08:00","id":311874,"title":"","content":"Oh god, no, the Dusk and Dawn Courts are based on Seelie/Unseelie, which is Slavic. Like, Norse-Slavic-Tolkien-Is-Gonna-Start-Writing-Fanfiction-This-Is-Definitely-Not-Native-American<br /> <br /> The closest we have for in-game canon for things like this is a subset of differently named Courts that are basically the seasonal Courts. Seasonal works really well for Native American freeholds too. They're under the &quot;Faraway Courts&quot; in Winter Masques, and are basically based around &quot;What is the most resounding aspect of this time frame?&quot; Dead Season/Long Winter, Dry Season, etc. Basically, you just pick whatever actually happens in the area. For a really temperate climate, you might only have Wet and Dry seasons, while for somewhere on the coast, you have Hurricane Season, and whatnot.<br /> <br /> I'd avoid focusing too much on Native American freeholds as &quot;ancient&quot; or &quot;lost&quot; though, because a lot of Native American practices are still actually a thing today, and that would presumably go for freeholds based in Native American culture as well. These cultures are still alive!<br /> <br /> Of course, anything based on Atlantis is up for grabs. . . .<br /> <br /> And it's been brought up in this thread already, but myths and stories about the fae exist all over the world. Basically, anything that isn't outright a spirit, demon, or angel is pretty much guaranteed to be a faerie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T00:11:46-08:00","id":312019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-chan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/299763-native-american-changelings?p=311874#post311874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd avoid focusing too much on Native American freeholds as &quot;ancient&quot; or &quot;lost&quot; though, because a lot of Native American practices are still actually a thing today, and that would presumably go for freeholds based in Native American culture as well. These cultures are still alive!</div> </div> </div> </div>Mine idea was not &quot;all Native American changelings are long lost&quot;. Only in this particular town, in the middle of nowhere, Arcadian Huntmsan have out hunt them centuries ago, just like colonists freehold, few centuries later. In <b>this region</b>, not in all Americas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T00:27:48-08:00","id":312031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-chan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/299763-native-american-changelings?p=311874#post311874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh god, no, the Dusk and Dawn Courts are based on Seelie/Unseelie, which is Slavic. Like, Norse-Slavic-Tolkien-Is-Gonna-Start-Writing-Fanfiction-This-Is-Definitely-Not-Native-American</div> </div> </div> </div>Seelie/Unseelie are Scottish. Tolkein drew on Celtic and Germanic Myth. All of which are completely different from Slavic (Eastern European and Russian).<br /> <br /> The Sun and Moon Courts in CtL are Slavic (based partially on the false notion that Slavic Myth was heavily dualistic. It was not - that was a Christian scholar assumption upon translating the name Chernobog [Black God], that there must be a Belobog [White God]). The Scottish Seelie and Unseelie Courts have been stated to be Spring-Summer and Autumn-Winter alliances.<br /> <br /> The Dawn and Dusk Courts found in &quot;Swords at Dawn&quot; and &quot;Dancers in the Dusk&quot; do not have strong cultural associations, though I can definitely see Norse Mythic elements in the Dusk Court.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T04:20:06-08:00","id":312141,"title":"","content":"I like Sun and Moon better as Seelie and Unseelie than an attempt at Slavic myth. I also prefer Day and Night, just to keep with other sorts of conventions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T19:21:13-08:00","id":312703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/299763-native-american-changelings?p=312019#post312019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mine idea was not &quot;all Native American changelings are long lost&quot;. Only in this particular town, in the middle of nowhere, Arcadian Huntmsan have out hunt them centuries ago, just like colonists freehold, few centuries later. In <b>this region</b>, not in all Americas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I guess that does sound like it could build a rather foreboding tone into the setting -- sorry if I jumped the gun on that then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seelie/Unseelie are Scottish. Tolkein drew on Celtic and Germanic Myth. All of which are completely different from Slavic (Eastern European and Russian).<br /> <br /> The Sun and Moon Courts in CtL are Slavic (based partially on the false notion that Slavic Myth was heavily dualistic. It was not - that was a Christian scholar assumption upon translating the name Chernobog [Black God], that there must be a Belobog [White God]). The Scottish Seelie and Unseelie Courts have been stated to be Spring-Summer and Autumn-Winter alliances.<br /> <br /> The Dawn and Dusk Courts found in &quot;Swords at Dawn&quot; and &quot;Dancers in the Dusk&quot; do not have strong cultural associations, though I can definitely see Norse Mythic elements in the Dusk Court..</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, you're right, my bad, again! Aaah, that was really incorrect on what &quot;Slavic&quot; was too, thank you for the correction @_@<br /> <br /> I wasn't aware that there was a write-up for actual Dawn/Dusk Courts -- I thought that was just one of the &quot;also known as&quot; monikers for Sun/Moon. Thank you for the information.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm sorry for such an incorrect post u-u;;;;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T13:49:02-08:00","id":313269,"title":"","content":"It should also be noted that a good half of indigenous mythology (from almost any tribe) involves a tribe member wandering &quot;just over the mountains&quot; or &quot;across a mysterious river&quot; or &quot;through a dangerous trip,&quot; only to meet a very strange people, like giants the size of mountains, or people who have stone orbs for faces, or a people who ride ducks into battle, or a place where everyone dresses as an animal and does animal things and all the animals dress like people and do people things, then that tribe member coming back and having strange and mysterious wisdom or knowledge.<br /> <br /> Native Changelings might also use a slightly different lexicon: they might use &quot;Clan&quot; for Seeming and/or Kith, and directly refer to themselves as being that thing which their features represent. That leechfinger is an evil hunger witch, and tries to play the part, even if she's really a nice person. The soldier is a great hero and bowman, and despite his reservations that heroes have a place in the modern world, he still finds monsters to slay. The skittering, poisonous Beast is Spider, and she does her best - dressing like a man, tempting people to get drunk, and stealing sacred food.<br /> <br /> Most of my table is indigenous - Muskokee, Seminole, Iroquois, Apache, and Hawai'ian, and most of them grew up around their stories rather tightly. So those themes tend to sneak into our Changeling games more often than not - the rule of four, oral tansference of Contracts, shells and rugs as common tokens, ability to acquire Glamour through complex rituals, metaphor animals as second-order simulacra, and a complete discard of the in-book court system for a home-brew directional/color-based court, which has, over its lifetime, cribbed from the invading European changelings a little here and there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T14:33:44-08:00","id":313303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>raygungoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/299763-native-american-changelings?p=313269#post313269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of my table is indigenous - Muskokee, Seminole, Iroquois, Apache, and Hawai'ian, and most of them grew up around their stories rather tightly. So those themes tend to sneak into our Changeling games more often than not - the rule of four, oral tansference of Contracts, shells and rugs as common tokens, ability to acquire Glamour through complex rituals, metaphor animals as second-order simulacra, and a complete discard of the in-book court system for a home-brew directional/color-based court, which has, over its lifetime, cribbed from the invading European changelings a little here and there.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Raygungoth</b>, I would love to hear more about it. Especially your homebrew directional/color courts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T22:34:50-08:00","id":313509,"title":"","content":"Sacred Hoop Courts - based around the symbol of the hoop or ring in many mythologies and finalized during the Wokova metempsychosis (the Great Ghost Dance) in the 1800s as a sort of pan-Indian dance and faith system built around modules of oral stories that could be transmitted and used as the giving clan o tribe saw fit. So, here's some bare minimum stuff.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">North/White Court</span>:</b> The Court of the White Buffalo, The White Court, The Court of Stars, The Many-Spangled, The Court of Death<br /> &quot;<i>Who I <b>was</b> no longer matters, only who I will <b>become</b></i>.&quot;<br /> They escaped from Arcadia only to realize that in so doing, they had become someone else. Like peeling away a scab, the pain was worth the payoff. White is the color of death and renewal. White of snow, white of bones, and white of ash in a fire pit. The White Court sees all things as holding a boundless potential, even the end. Every story must stop, and only eternity holds any ultimate sadness. They believe that their former lives were the price of admission into the world in which they have been born anew.<br /> <br /> Their court emotion is <b>Catharsis</b>. It is a sort of purity, a blazing, unsullied star that is more of a starting point than anything else. It is the relaxed freshness of arrival home after a long trip, the sensation of sweet air on one's face after an eternity in sweaty darkness, and the releasing ache of the muscles on the verge of sleep or the slow contentment of waking. A scab is terrible to ha<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">ve, but the sensation of it finally coming off is freeing and exhilarating. Thus, the sensation is not one of sadness, not quite happiness, but instead an unsullied state the represents the transition into another emotion. The calm after a runner's high or the unbridled relief felt when danger has finally passed is a specialty of the court, and the purest form of the catharsis they seek to retain.</span></span><br /> <br /> As the northern mantle progresses, the changeling begins to look more distant and stellar. At low mantle, the changeling may exhibit one or two points of light, like stars, following them or adorning their person. At higher levels, the changeling may experience other changes, such as hair turning white, eyes turning the dark color of night, ash clinging to the body or face, blowing on the wind, or dusting the changeling's boots. Eventually, the changeling may turn all they touch white with smears of sand or dust, with large white patterns dancing across their clothing.<br /> <b>Mantle</b> (\u25cf): The changeling gains a +1 bonus to all Occult pools.<br /> <b>Mantle</b> (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf): The white courtier gains a 2-die bonus to Resolve, Stamina, and Composure rolls to resist supernatural abilities. In addition, the changeling treats his resistance traits as two dots higher when subtracting them from the die pool for supernatural abilities used on him that subtract a resistance trait from their activation roll.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Mantle</b> (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf): Once per day, the changeling can re-roll any Contract activation roll. The results of the second roll stand.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Contracts: </b>Northern Star, White Rattle, Spell</span></span>bound Sky<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">East/Blue Court</span>:</b> The New Court, The Blue Court, The Court of Sudden Strikes, The Empowered Thinkers<br /> &quot;<i>On the one hand, I have crawled through Hell back into the light. On the other, now I need to find a challenge even greater</i>.&quot;<br /> Blue court sees their time in Arcadia as a challenge from a stronger force and a driving force for them to change, adapt, and become stronger in the crucibles it offered. Unturned stones bear no treasure, and while the downside is that there's sometimes a rattlesnake down there, it's the drive to discovery and the need to top the next challenge that makes them who they are. They accept that their time has changed them, and dwell on it constantly, sometimes leading to deep depression, but always grinding their teeth into the newest challenges to their psyche. It takes those changelings who approach their situation with a scientific bent, testing themselves and others with elaborate games or experiments, and those who want to do nothing more than meddle in the affairs of others with intent to improve them or disavow them of their deeply held beliefs. The changeling who openly mocks Christianity or the changeling who sets up pranks with friends are the types who come easily to the Eastern Court. There are violent individuals who also come to the court, mostly to test themselves among the constant struggle for power among them.<br /> <br /> Their court emotion is best described as <b>Hardship</b>. It's not anger so much as it is the ability to take it all in such that your body seems overwhelmed by the task but still excited by the possibilitie<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">s of solving all those problems and either dives into a haze of joy or collapses under the strain. From hardship, our lives are filled with illumination, through clarity caused by understanding what opposes us, we become more than who we are. Some members of the group inflict suffering upon themselves, or provide challenges for others, becoming their villains and rivals in an attempt to spur them on to better things. They tend to have a reputation for being extreme sports fanatics and short-sighted thrillseekers pushing the next extreme sport to the limit, but they're more likely to be found in laboratories and classrooms or on open fields of challenge pushing themselves and others ever-harder for a goal they can't even nail down for themselves.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">At a low mantle rating, the Eastern Courtier seems a little grating, their presence somewhat uncomfortable and tinged with some vitalizing force that seems to exist merely to get under the viewer's skin. As the mantle grows in power, it tinges the Changeling with blue and turquoise gemstones, painting blue marks on their skin or clothes, surrounding them with the smell of coffee or soft, powdery smells, growing seals of the court's animals on their aura and cutting the Changeling a sharp outline among the world.<br /> <b>Mantle (\u25cf):</b> The changeling gains +1 to all Perception rolls.<br /> <b>Mantle (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf):</b> Once per day, the changeling can focus her efforts to gain a +3 dice bonus to any one action.<br /> <b>Mantle (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf):</b> Once per combat, if the changeling is unseen by his opponents, he can tap one opponent with a stick and shout. He can continue to do this, and each time he does this before actually attacking the opponent, the changeling regains one glamour and can add a +1 bonus to all his attack rolls against that opponent for the scene. The changeling must be under the effects of no protective contracts save for those that grant stealth bonuses when he approaches his opponent in order for this to work.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Contracts: </b>Eastern Ribbon, Blue Axe, Ashen Earth</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">South/Green Court:</span></b> The Blazing Court, The Court of Open Doors, The Honorable Ones, The Green Court<br /> &quot;<i>You have to know the rules, follow the rules, otherwise things get ugly</i>.&quot;<br /> You can trust a contract to be followed to the letter. You can trust the bonds of a promise to work as it wills. You can trust the world to try to yank everything out from under you, and you can trust yourself to come out stronger. To the Blazing Court, they place their trust in laws, in the world around them, and the world which they've placed themselves. Bargains and pledges are nothing more than absolute trust in the ironclad terms of the obligations spelled out within them. This is the firm belief of the Green Court, that in the bare truth of a matter, anything can be learned.<br /> <br /> There comes, with <b>Trust</b>, also a faith. Unlike the faith that drives the Red Ones, the Southern trust is in objects and laws. Intangible things such as contracts, and any system composed of parts that works the same way every time. What then, of the unexpected? Of course, any system has the right to a few quirks here and there, so trust is never absolute, that's a fool's errand and leads to a quick death. The old Southern courtier gets other people to trust in her and her abilities. There comes with it a certain freedom from the True Fae in that the Green courtiers can place their trust in others, to release themselves into the control of another, that gives even the most hardened turncoats moments of pause.<br /> <br /> As the Green mantle grows, the changeling begins to glimmer with a turquoise sheen. Perhaps her jewelry looks like jade or other green stones, or her eyes flash green when she blinks. Her seeming might develop a little feathery cap like a woodpecker, and she may seem youthful and innocent. As the seeming grows, her aura may flash with the colors of the bright sun, be surrounded by the smell of warm popcorn, the crack of a baseball bat, and be adorned with all manner of green jewels.<br /> <b>Mantle (\u25cf): </b>The changeling gains a +1 bonus to all Persuasion rolls.<br /> <b>Mantle (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf):</b> The changeling gains a +1 bonus to Clarity rolls and tests for degeneration if anyone she trusts is able to comfort or witness her.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Mantle (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf): </b>The changeling refills her entire glamour pool when she gets someone to completely and implicitly trust her. By the same token, when that same trust is broken, and the changeling betrays their confidence, even accidentally, the changeling's glamour pool empties out and they suffer a Clarity violation (two dice).</span></span><br /> <b>Contracts: </b>Southern Seal, Green Knife, The Quiet Sea<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">West/Red Court:</span></b> The Red Court, The Tired Court, The Court of Clenched Jaws, The Court of Stoicism, The Old Fellows<br /> &quot;<i>Winds coming from </i>inside <i>the trees today. Think I'll go for a walk in the woods.</i>&quot;<br /> Some changelings escaped and were ecstatic at reaching their new lifes, others felt the need to test themselves and others forever, so that they would be stronger when the evil came back for them, and others seek the need to trust their world again. The Red Court spits a line in the sand, turns around to face Arcadia, and buries his feet in the dirt. &quot;Come and get me,&quot; they say. You won't like it. They draw a line at the boundaries of the Hedge and forever prepare themselves for the inevitable arrival of their old masters, and they will not allow those masters a reprieve.<br /> <br /> At first glance, the stoic <b>Resolve</b> of the court is a good thing. They stand firm. They have their beliefs and they stick to them. The trouble comes when the belief is clearly wrong, but as a matter of the court's philosophy, it is right to them. To become resolute, you must be absolutely right in what you believe, to the point of turning to face the True Fae should they come calling and you still tell them \u201cno more\u201d to their faces. This can have other detrimental effects than the obvious: a changeling's ties to its mortal faith become ever stronger. They are not concerned so much with the truth as their neighbor, only in what they believe is right, and they will lose their feet rather than change that belief. A changeling could be a liberal defender of the people while <span style=\"font-size:12px\">another could be a mad Baptist preacher, but unchanging and unyielding in their <span style=\"font-family:arial\">beliefs.<br /> <br /> As the Evening Mantle grows, the changeling becomes covered in red tracery; symbols that look to be made of red silk or even wet blood begin adorning the changeling's clothes, starting out as thin marks and becoming more complex as the Lost becomes more in tune with the west. She may take on a red hue as if lit by the setting sun.<br /> <b>Mantle (\u25cf):</b> The changeling can spend a point of Willpower to gain four dice for heroic effort rather than three when a penalty is going to be applied to the roll.<br /> <b>Mantle (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf):</b> The changeling benefits from 1 point of armor.<br /> <b>Mantle (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf): </b>The changeling may reroll any failed resistance roll once per story. You must use the results of the second roll.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Contracts: </b>Western Heart, Red River, Unyielding Flame</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","user":"raygungoth","date":". 11-16-2014, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T01:48:52-08:00","id":313567,"title":"","content":"Now I want to add some real ancient Native American changelings to the game. Great stuff, man! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T13:39:12-08:00","id":313932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/299763-native-american-changelings?p=313567#post313567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I want to add some real ancient Native American changelings to the game. Great stuff, man! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Somewhere around here I have material for &quot;Atomic City,&quot; a (heavily) fictionalized version of the town in Idaho the I use as my primary Changeling/Promethean/Demon town.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T16:44:24-08:00","id":314036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>raygungoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/299763-native-american-changelings?p=313509#post313509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beautiful things</div> </div> </div> </div>This is AWESOME! How do they share power? Have you written their Contracts out, or are they just ideas? Care to share?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T10:56:46-08:00","id":314678,"title":"","content":"<u><b>ATOMIC CITY FREEHOLD</b></u><br /> <u><b>-or-</b></u><br /> <u><b>The Law of the Sacred Hoop in Atomic City</b></u><br /> est. May 17, 1953<br /> <br /> We come together under the Sacred Hoop and this circle of stones to conceive of a new Freehold under the auspices of the gathered People who have come before us. To ensure domestic tranquility amongst ourselves and those members of our body, to promote the welfare and secure prosperity in our new lives, establish this fragment of the Sacred Hoop here in Atomic City and its environs, to be known as Atomic City Freehold.<br /> <br /> This document does not constitute a Pledge, but outlines provisions to be enforced under the sufferance of law outside Court Pledges.<br /> <br /> <b>Establishment of Representation</b><br /> <br /> There shall, in accordance to the law of the Scared Hoop, be formed Four Courts. The Four Courts shall follow the four directions and their sacred enumerations, and from them shall be formed each their own individual judiciary discretion, to be represented among the Four Courts, and duly beholden to the decisions of a representative committee formed of no more than five individuals, one of each Court and one independent person not beholden to the laws of these Courts. Each Court shall have its own choice in the member applied to this judiciary committee, and this committee's purpose shall be levying and interpreting the laws as they apply to the Atomic City Freehold.<br /> <br /> As this assembled congress believes in freedom of choice and peace herein, let it be known that no Lost shall be without succor within this freehold. Whereas, in accordance with the desire for personal liberty, let no Lost be directly beholden, through pledge, to uphold the law of this Freehold of Atomic City, in accordance with the Law of the Sacred Hoop, though in refusing to uphold these laws may they be branded with the marks of their transgression as punishment in addition to whatever levied penalty be applied by the judicial power of the Atomic City Freehold.<br /> <br /> An independent person is hereby defined as an individual dwelling with the environs of Atomic City but not beholden directly to this document, and as such includes any ensorcelled mortal not beholden to the Pledge of any given Court, any member of a Court not counted among the Sacred Hoop, or an individual designated as independent by the house committee as defined below. An independent person is granted full and applicable protection under the establishments and regulations herein as it pertains to the Sacred Hoop, though they may not be privy to individual Contracts, Pledges, or special knowledge confined to an individual Court, provided that special knowledge might impact a decision they may be required to make in the due course of executive or judiciary power.<br /> <br /> <b>Establishment of House Committee</b><br /> <br /> Here we gathered establish that an executive House Committee shall be made up of two representative individuals of each of the Four Courts, numbered eight in total, and two independent persons, named hereafter as the House Committee. This House Committee shall be headed by a primary speaker and legislator with the power to formally introduce legislation, tally votes, and construct new offices as required, hereafter referred to as the Executive Director. Each decision prepared and passed by the House Committee cannot be enacted upon without majority consent of this chamber and the Chamber of the Four Courts, to be established below.<br /> <br /> <b>The Chamber of the Four Courts</b><br /> <br /> Each of the Four Courts must possess a chamber composed of a single representative in which executive power over their Court is invested, called President of Court. Each court shall hold this person through both word of law and general appointment by a majority of Beholden individuals, as defined by any individual under the Pledge of that Court. Each four years, a new President of Court shall be appointed, beginning one year after the establishment of this document for the White Court, two years after the establishment of this document for the Blue Court, three years after the establishment of this document for the Green Court, and four years after the establishment of this document for the Red Court.<br /> <br /> Upon six months before election for President of Court, general elections are to be held among the Court in regards to House Committee representatives, who will then vote on judiciary representatives as outlined previously among those candidates apportioned by the President of Court. As well, each President of Court may choose a Second should they removed from term before election terms are complete. A President of Court may only serve two terms consecutively, though after a period of one term has passed, their service may be re-entered through election as though they had not previously served.<br /> <br /> Each President of Court shall have the power to appoint or call for votes to appoint individual treasurers, ambassadors, and other offices for which the Court has use. The President of Court may possess individual powers among their respective Court, including but not limited to calling armies or militias into the service of the Sacred Hoop or Atomic City Freehold, make treaties among other Courts but not Court Systems, give a State of the Court among peers and the public, and recommend to the House Committee measures that they judge necessary and expedient. The President of Court may receive ambassadors and other public ministers as appropriate, and be, as any civil officer of the Atomic City Freehold, removed from office upon conviction of treason, bribery, or other high crimes.<br /> <br /> <b>Establishment of Law</b><br /> <br /> The following shall apply to any Court, regardless of legislation.<br /> <br /> <b>The First (Provision of High Treason):</b> Any individual, free, independent, or otherwise, who is convicted of aiding an entity of the Hedge in locating, abducting, or controlling any individual through direct assistance is likewise convicted of High Treason.<br /> <br /> <b>The Second (Provision for Fetch-Killing and Impersonation):</b> Accomplished, planned murder of any individual posing as or thought to be posed of the likeness of any other individual requires the permission of the individual therefore personified by the likeness, else three tasks as decided by the judiciary committee, to be drawn from a list submitted by the individual personified by the likeness.<br /> <br /> <b>The Third (Provision of Wartime Aid):</b> Any individual providing aid to combat any hostile entity which resides primarily in the Hedge, whether by direct or indirect action, is a lawful member of the Atomic City Freehold. Any individual refusing to do so publicly is hereby considered an unlawful citizen and subject to the whims of the judiciary committee as having committed a public misdemeanor.<br /> <br /> <b>The Fourth (Provision for Dueling): </b>Acts of violent intent must be either unplanned and reserved for acts of self preservation as to be defined by the circumstances of their occurrence, or else be scheduled with the Committee among the individual Court(s) to which the duelists are beholden by Pledge.<br /> <br /> <b>The Fifth (Provision of Pledge):</b> Any Court within this Atomic City Freehold is fully authorized in the utilization of Pledges to induct its members under their provisions of law or enforce the law as outlined under the auspices of their individual Court, provided that they do not conflict with the Establishment of Law.<br /> <br /> <b>The Sixth (Provision of Nobility):</b> No member of this Atomic City Freehold is capable of providing a title of Nobility. No title of Nobility shall be required for an office or holding within Atomic City Freehold, nor shall any Noble title be recognized outside of an ambassadorial or representative capacity.<br /> <br /> _________________________________<br /> <br /> <br /> I'll see if I can dig up the contracts. I think most of them were just hotfixes, but I'll see what I can do, or write them out more clearly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T15:09:47-08:00","id":315713,"title":"","content":"Found some of the contracts! White Court first.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Contracts of the Northern Star</b></u><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>That Which Has Been Lost (\u25cf)</b></span> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">With this Contract, the changeling touches a subject on the shoulder and attempts to discover something that has been left behind, something that the subject either wishes to cleanse from themselves, forgetting it, or get back. This could be homesickness, a treasured item, a person, or even a particular emotion or sight.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> <b>Cost: </b>1 Glamour<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wyrd + Empathy - victim's Resolve<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Catch:</b> What the person has lost is within sight of the subject.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Roll Results<br /> Dramatic Failure:</b> The changeling catches a flash of their own past in Arcadia, and suffers a -1 penalty to all social rolls for the scene.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The changeling cannot determine the subject's past.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Success:</b> The changeling sees an event or item the character left behind in their past. It could be something they miss, but it could be something they don't care about anymore; in either case, the changeling understands that, as well.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The changeling also gains insight into what made the person leave their past behind them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Learning to Let Go (\u25cf\u25cf)</b></span> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Part of the Court of Purity is in releasing people from their past burdens, making the soil new for growth to begin again. This clause helps the changeling suppress emotional ties to people and objects for a time, however briefly, allowing one to act free of it, or even experience a brief moment without it weighing upon them. This clause can be dangerous when invoked, so it is used somewhat sparingly, but it is simultaneously a great boon.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> Mantle (North) (\u25cf) or Court Goodwill (North) (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> <b>Cost: </b>2 Glamour<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wyrd + Empathy + Mantle (North) - victim's Composure<br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended (threshold equal to the subject's Willpower)<br /> <b>Catch:</b> The changeling is helping the subject forget emotional ties to the changeling.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Roll Results<br /> Dramatic Failure:</b> The changeling makes the memory stronger, and experiences it with the victim. The changeling is worse off, and immediately acquires a temporary derangement that lasts a scene.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Failure:</b> The changeling cannot help the subject, and must begin again.<br /> <b>Success:</b> Progress is made. When enough successes are accrued, the changeling grants the subject the ability to re-roll a failed degeneration roll made in the previous scene, potentially preventing loss of Clarity or Integrity. This clause can also be used to suppress a derangement acquired from a loss of Clarity or Morality for a scene, if it is too late to reconcile the past completely. It cannot suppress Frailties gained from Clarity loss.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Exceptional Success:</b> The changeling also grants a +1 bonus on the new roll.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Becoming Unclouded (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</b></span> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">With this clause, the White Courtier burns away his past entirely, effectively becoming a new person for a short time, seeing the world with a new perspective, whether good or ill. This new perspective lets the changeling see a problem from an entirely new angle.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> Mantle (North) (\u25cf\u25cf) or Court Goodwill (North) (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> <b>Cost: </b>2 Glamour<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wyrd + Expression<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Catch:</b> The changeling is away from the company of friends or anyone who can help him remember who he is.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Roll Results<br /> Dramatic Failure:</b> The changeling becomes so mired in herself that she sits down on the spot and reflects on her past, overcome with grief over what she has lost.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> Nothing happens; the changeling cannot put himself out of his old mindset.<br /> <b>Success:</b> This clause allows the changeling to roll again for any mental roll that does not allow multiple tries, and may allow the changeling to completely forget a slight or other personal peeve that is currently bothering her; this clause instantly counteracts magic that is affecting the changeling's emotions. In the meantime, the changeling has selective amnesia; he does not know what sort of physical or social skills he might possess, and can only make new rolls for mental skills made earlier in the scene.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The changeling can apply a -2 penalty to one of his mental skills to acquire a +2 bonus to any other mental skill for the rest of the scene.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Dredging Up Pain (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</span></b> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">The past is painful; that's one of the reasons it's often left behind. This clause allows the changeling to draw up a painful memory, forcing a victim to relive the incident or become obsessed by it.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> Mantle (North) (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) or Court Goodwill (North) (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Cost: </b>3 Glamour<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wyrd + Empathy + Mantle (North) - victim's Composure<br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended (threshold equal to the subject's Willpower)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Catch:</b> The changeling is holding a diary or other such record of the subject's past and presents it to the air, holding it up over their head.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Roll Results<br /> Dramatic Failure:</b> The changeling suffers a flash of her own experiences in Arcadia and hears the voice of her own Keeper, and suffers an immediate Clarity roll (roll three dice).<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The changeling can't find anything she can amplify or afflict on the target.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The changeling amplifies one of the subject's past painful memories; the changeling has no control over which memory is dredged up unless he knows the specific memory he wants to bring up. The target immediately begins suffering from a severe derangement. Changelings afflicted by this clause tend to either flee or stand in place, shivering, but will fight back if touched or moved, as they experience their durance once again. Using this clause on changelings can potentially cause Clarity loss for the user.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The changeling gets a sense of what the memory they have dredged up happens to be, seeing in play out before them as their victim interacts with it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Past Catches Up (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</span></b> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">With this clause, the past becomes a real and tangible thing, or else fading into obscurity, allowing the changeling to eliminate it utterly or make it catch up to their victim, confronting them directly. This clause cannot be used unless the changeling knows the person or object they wish to scour or to call up.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> Mantle (North) (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> <b>Cost: </b>2 Glamour + 1 Willpower<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wyrd + Expression + Mantle (North) \u2013 Victim's Resolve<br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended (threshold equal to twice the subject's Willpower)<br /> <b>Catch:</b> The changeling is using this clause on a willing subject to scour the past.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Roll Results<br /> Dramatic Failure:</b> One of the changeling's own pasts comes catching up to them just as if they were the subject. Note that the Keeper is in the changeling's past.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Failure:</b> The changeling fails to make progress toward the goal.<br /> <b>Success:</b> Progress is made. When enough successes are accrued, the changeling must touch their target with a coup stick and whisper a clue to the subject as to what's happening. Within the next day, an item or person that the subject has left behind in their past and severed all ties to comes catching up. They run across the item at a garage sale, the person rolls into town, the FBI discovers clues that implicate them in a crime they've committed, and so on. If the changeling wishes to scour a past, the subject loses all contact with the item or person or event. The FBI loses information, the item is lost or stolen, the person leaves town or the subject loses phone numbers and e-mail addresses. The subject can recover the item with an extended Wits + Investigation roll, with a threshold equal to the changeling's successes, and an interval of one day.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Exceptional Success:</b> The changeling also knows precisely when and where the person or item will be when the subject encounters it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> Contracts of the White Rattle<br /> (these were essentially like Eternal Spring with alternate names; i was going to change all the catches, but haven't yet)<br /> Good Night's Rest (\u25cf)<br /> Catch: The subject is preparing for something important such as a test, lengthy repair work, or day labor, and is losing sleep over it.<br /> Opening up the Sky (\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> The Secret of Medicine (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> Welcome to the New Age (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> Close to the Forest (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> <br /> Contracts of the Spellbound Sky<br /> only person who played a White courtier was a Darkling Spider-type who was focused on talecrafting and elemental contracts<br /> these contracts would directly deal with some pretty random crap, but they'd also do stuff like tell you what contracts have been used in the area, what a particular token does, or how to find something magical you're looking for","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T21:16:14-08:00","id":315881,"title":"","content":"Great, great stuff Raygungoth! I've cut and pasted it all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}